Why: The in-place 32/64-bit conversions of tools_common.F
 (MUMPS_ICOPY_32TO64_64C_IP_REC, MUMPS_ICOPY_64TO32_64C_IP_REC and their
 REAL counterparts) pass an element of an INTEGER (REAL) array to an
 INTEGER(8) (DOUBLE PRECISION) dummy, a type mismatch rejected by
 gfortran >= 10. The 64-bit half is now passed through a pointer of the
 right type created with C_F_POINTER on the same storage (the array gains
 the TARGET attribute); the generated code is unchanged.
Upstream: not sent; worth offering.
Obsolete when: upstream changes these routines.

diff --git a/src/tools_common.F b/src/tools_common.F
index 6a75b04..ca22989 100644
--- a/src/tools_common.F
